{"c":[{"id":"d86d11223c1303db","sum":"B13-B14: SnippetLedger charges a text to every window showing it; Jev replays vary ~3 fields, so rerun before reading a delta; socket tests bind to their own HelperServer; load-proof tests fix the generator clock; every stop carries stopReason; dry-run replays with an oracle Jev.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"ea5143bf5e6179f1","sum":"B13-B14: SnippetLedger over all windows charges a text to every window showing it; kindless fill fields withheld only on related cuts; live Jev replays vary about 3 fields, rerun before trusting a delta; socket tests bind publish to that test's own HelperServer.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"15d4fcad6f30cb62","sum":"SnippetLedger over model.windows.values() charges a taken text to every window showing it, either way round, and refuses if any is over budget; a kindless fill field is withheld only on cuts of typed values or its label words, never on any cut (B13).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T075125Z-769f076b2b26d50b","text":"SnippetLedger(windows) charges a taken text to every window that shows it, either way round (line inside the text, or text inside a line); refuses when any of them is over budget. Build it over model.windows.values(), never just the source window (B13).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T075154Z-10f895f4b8d309e7","text":"A fill field whose label names no kind is withheld when a cut took a typed value or a cut conversation left out a line sharing its label words; withholding it on any cut blanked Name on the fill desk (unrelated team chat always cut) and lost the first-look offer (B13 live-final).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"be073912f9f26071","sum":"Live Jev replays vary by about 3 fields run to run (24-27 of 78, B13): rerun before reading a delta. Socket tests bind publish/sendToReader to the HelperServer made in that beforeEach, or a late 'stopped' leaks into the next test (B14).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T075211Z-5ac7a437648ff4d5","text":"Live replay noise: the same code gave 24, 26, 27 and 25 of 78 on 'sources in Messages' rule on (B13); pre-ask withholding is deterministic, so differences under about 3 fields are Jev answering differently. Rerun part with --variants/--rules/--fixes before reading a delta.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T100918Z-34fd442f4a978ffa","text":"Socket test harnesses must bind the helper's publish/sendToReader to the HelperServer made in that beforeEach, not the reassigned server variable: an earlier test's run timed out 5 s later and its 'stopped id-1' reached a later test's host (B13's flake, fixed B14).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"7d2825e282ce0f8d","sum":"B14: fix the generator clock with setGeneratorClock(() => 0) in load-proof tests; names are withheld only on namesCut; every stopped taskProgress carries stopReason; try a copy of live-replay.ts with an oracle Jev before a live replay.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"b51bc99b3aa533a8","sum":"B14: load-proof tests fix the generator clock with setGeneratorClock(() => 0) (find exposed ones with a wall clock jumping 1 s per read); a name field is withheld only on namesCut, since counting names prose mentions blanked Full name on Messages sets.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T100918Z-d51f417a758957f9","text":"Tests whose answers must not depend on CPU load fix the generator's budget clock with setGeneratorClock(() => 0) (candidates.ts); find exposed tests by making the wall clock jump 1 s per read and rerunning the suite (B14).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T100919Z-90979468cad825fe","text":"Names are a fill kind (kinds.ts NAME_TERM): a field that takes a name is withheld only when namesCut (name-like lines or a contact line's names kept out, a partway cap/clock stop, cutAll); counting names that prose mentions blanked Full name on every Messages set (B14).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"d0f5d3ab6d535ae7","sum":"B14: a stopped taskProgress carries stopReason (stops go through stopped(reason); TaskProgress is a zod union on phase); before a live replay, run a copy of live-replay.ts with an oracle Jev to see withholding and wrong fills for free.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T100919Z-9bbdea6cd359a808","text":"A stopped taskProgress must carry stopReason: executor progress() refuses 'stopped' at type level and stops go through stopped(reason); TaskProgress is a zod union on phase so the exported JSON Schema states the rule (B14).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T100919Z-aefa98c201821a3a","text":"Before a live replay, copy live-replay.ts with an oracle Jev (gold if offered, else a name-like decoy) to see withholding and wrong fills for free; B14's copy is ~/.caret-run/evidence/screen/b14/oracle/oracle-replay.ts.txt.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"09651b924661b23f","sum":"B15-B17: acts need an actGrant, revoked by any pause/stop; Chrome's web AX tree is late and ignores AXSelectedText(Range); background WKWebView drops writes; rebundle the fixture after builds; event cards judge a body's last sentence; tests over 4 offers/hour use eager.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"d8e5e429dbcf056a","sum":"B15 (updated B22): the reader acts only under an actGrant from an accepted offer, revoked at once by any pause, stop or take over; Chrome builds web AX trees late and ignores AXSelectedText; background WKWebView drops writes; the walk check catches drops.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"166b843e5f81c9fe","sum":"B15: any pause, stop or take over revokes the act grant at once (fakes refuse acts without one only under enforceGrants); Chrome builds its web AX tree seconds late, so wait for the form's fields in the model before acting.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T124042Z-0ff3662999b3099a","text":"A stop or takeOver revokes the task's act grant at once, so a write still on its way is refused and the run ends as stopped by you; test fakes (FakeApp, SocketReader) refuse acts without a grant only when enforceGrants is set.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T124042Z-b3569a4cf63d6bee","text":"Chrome builds its web AX tree seconds after the reader asks for it: wait until the form's fields are in the screen model before acting, or the first plans stop with target-not-found (B15 explore run).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"ead499ab30c4256f","sum":"B15: the reader acts only under an actGrant (task, pid, window; 120 s, monotonic) from an accepted offer. Chrome takes AXValue on web inputs but ignores AXSelectedText; background WKWebView drops writes; the executor's walk check catches each drop.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T124106Z-598a6c678d777d69","text":"caret-screen acts only under a helper actGrant (task, pid, window; 120 s max, monotonic); --act-pids is for fixture tests. Only accepted offers get grants (Executor.run opts.grant); a consumer runPlan never does, so the product refuses it (B15).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T124106Z-77698db11d4c9d42","text":"Real targets (B15): Chrome takes AXValue on web inputs, front or back, but answers AXSelectedText ok and changes nothing; WKWebView in background-only caret-fixture drops value and insert silently; TextEdit takes all. The executor's walk check caught each drop.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"20ef30b80edf7d92","sum":"B15-B17: Chrome ignores web AXSelectedTextRange (insert refused); rerun bundle-fixture.sh after fixture builds; event cards judge only a body's last sentence, sent as a change; Balanced allows 4 offers/hour, so tests needing more send level eager.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"d7fa6d069180cfdc","sum":"B15-B16: Chrome ignores AXSelectedTextRange writes on web inputs, so insert is refused there; caret-fixture cannot take the front from T3; rerun bundle-fixture.sh after any swift build that changes the fixture, or evals run the old one.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T135628Z-a8acf778077d3916","text":"Chrome ignores AXSelectedTextRange writes on web inputs (selection stays 0+0), so the insert fallback is refused there; and caret-fixture's 'activate legacy' cannot take the front from T3 Code, only from apps the eval launched (B15).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T145037Z-c765ed8386dc228d","text":"Evals exec CaretFixture.app, a copy of caret-fixture made by apps/screen-reader/scripts/bundle-fixture.sh: rerun it after every swift build that changes the fixture, or the eval runs the old one (B16 lost two planner cases to an 08:33 bundle).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"1148a14e8f8ea414","sum":"B17 socket tests: an event card judges only the last finished sentence, so a body ends with it and arrives as a change (empty first); Balanced allows 4 offers an hour, so a test needing a fifth sends level eager first.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T191104Z-3aee21889eca1d38","text":"Event cards judge only the last finished sentence of what is typed: a test body must end with the event sentence and arrive as a change (empty body first), or no attend question is asked (B17 privacy session).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T191104Z-a560fe18d0d7ba87","text":"Balanced allows 4 offers an hour (settings.ts LEVELS): a socket test that needs a fifth pop-up sends settings level eager first, or the gate silently holds it (B17).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
